* Responder's second call, filled in (NOTES.md #P12)

Phase 4 (lane D2). `later-rounds.bml` writes responder's second call with few
rows; the positions below get the rest of the booklet's methods, so that a
responder who invites, prefers or shows a long suit stays on the system.

** After 1M-1NT and opener's new suit

The 1NT response is 6--10. Responder passes with a fit for the new suit, gives
preference to opener's major with two cards (`later-rounds.bml`), raises the
new suit with five cards (four in hearts) and 8--10, invites with 2NT on a
maximum, and shows a six-card suit of his own at the two level with a weak
hand. The suit-length comparison says the pass is for the longer suit.

1M-1N-2m-
3m = {prio:2} 8--10 hcp, 5+m
  #STOP
2N = {prio:2} 10 hcp, 0--2M, 0--3m
  #STOP

1S-1N-2H-
3H = {prio:2} 8--10 hcp, 4+!h
  #STOP
2N = {prio:2} 10 hcp, 0--2!s, 0--3!h
  #STOP

1H-1N-2C-
2D = {prio:1} 6--9 hcp, 6+!d, 0--1!h
  #STOP

1S-1N-2C-
2D = {prio:1} 6--9 hcp, 6+!d, 0--1!s
  #STOP
2H = {prio:1} 6--9 hcp, 6+!h, 0--1!s
  #STOP

1S-1N-2D-
2H = {prio:1} 6--9 hcp, 6+!h, 0--1!s
  #STOP

** After a two-over-one response and opener's new suit

The two-over-one response is 10+ and forcing one round; with 10--12 responder
now gives preference to opener's major with a doubleton, raises the new suit
with four cards, rebids a six-card suit, or bids 2NT; with 13+ or three-card
support the game rows of `later-rounds.bml` apply.

1M-2X-2Y-
2M = {prio:3} 10--12 hcp, 2+M, 0--2M, 0--3Y, 0--5X
  #STOP
3Y = {prio:3} 10--12 hcp, 4+Y, 0--2M
  #STOP
3X = {prio:3} 10--12 hcp, 6+X, 0--2M
  #STOP
2N = {prio:2} 10--12 hcp, 0--2M
  #STOP

** After a one-level response and opener's lower new suit

`later-rounds.bml` (`after-low-new-suit`) and `rebids.bml` pass with a fit for
the new suit, prefer opener's first suit and invite with 2NT; responder with
four cards in the new suit and 10--12 (no three-card support for opener's
first suit) raises it to the three level instead, the booklet's invitational
raise.

1Y-1Z-2X-
3X = {prio:2} 10--12 hcp, 4+X, 0--2Y
  #STOP

** Opener's rebid after responder's forcing new suit over an overcall (P12 batch 5)

`competition.bml` pastes `rebid-over-new-suit` for some of these auctions; the
rest (the major openings, the two-level overcalls) get the same rebid here:
raise, notrump with a stopper, or the cheapest rebid of the opening suit.

1H-(1S)-2D-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=D \n=d \L=4 \R=2H

1H-(2C)-2S-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=S \n=s \L=3 \R=3H

1S-(2C)-2H-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=H \n=h \L=3 \R=2S

1H-(2D)-2S-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=S \n=s \L=3 \R=3H

1S-(2D)-2H-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=H \n=h \L=3 \R=2S

1D-(2C)-2H-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=H \n=h \L=3 \R=3D

1D-(2C)-2S-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=S \n=s \L=3 \R=3D

1C-(2D)-2H-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=H \n=h \L=3 \R=3C

1C-(2D)-2S-(P)-
#PASTE rebid-over-new-suit \N=S \n=s \L=3 \R=3C

After a double of our opening and responder's non-forcing two-level suit (6--10,
six cards) opener passes, or raises with three-card support and 16+; after
the single raise of a major he bids game with 17+.

1D-(D)-2C-(P)-
3C = {prio:1} 16+ hcp, 4+!c
  #STOP
#STOP

1D-(D)-2M-(P)-
3M = {prio:1} 16+ hcp, 3+M
  #STOP
#STOP

